---
title: French Onion Soup
description: An easy version of the French classic
source: 30 Minute Chef <urn:isbn:1902617134>
author: Dan Askham
course: Starter
servings: 4
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
prep time: 20m
cook time: 35m
cuisine: French
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- french
- starter
- vegetarian
- soup
- savoury
---

Peel and slice the @onions{6%medium} and @garlic{3%cloves}. Melt the @butter{30%g} and add the onions, garlic and @sugar{1%tsp}, stirring constantly over a moderate heat until the onions brown and soften. If the onions start to stick, reduce the heat.

When the onions are uniformly caramelized (after 10 to ~{15%minutes}), add the @red wine{1%glass} and boil for 2 to ~{3%minutes} to reduce it.

Add the @beef stock{855%ml}(or vegetable stock for vegetarian) and simmer for a further ~{10%minutes}. Add the @salt and @pepper to taste.

Serve topped with toasted @French bread{}(made into croutons), topped with @Gruyère cheese{100%g}(grated) and a sprinkling of @fresh parsley{}(chopped). To melt the cheese place soup in heatproof bowls under the grill for a few minutes before serving.